<attribute name="mainDescription" nodeId="a1a34186">&lt;p&gt;
    Review the business cutover window and cutover activities with service management teams and business leads.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    Assess important criteria such as&amp;nbsp;site readiness, sponsor and stakeholder engagement, cutover communications,
    technology&amp;nbsp;infrastructure and business continuity plans.&amp;nbsp;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    Define the approach and criteria and review with key stakeholders.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    Readiness criteria listed&amp;nbsp;on a typical business preparedness checklist&amp;nbsp;include:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Is each site fully staffed, trained, and engaged?
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Are the sponsorship and stakeholders engaged?
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Are the sponsorship and stakeholders prepared and equipped for their roles in the cutover?
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Are all critical business leaders informed about the timing of checkpoints and go/no decision points?
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Have all necessary communications occurred? 
        &lt;ul&gt;
            &lt;li&gt;
                Memorandum to all department heads and offices
            &lt;/li&gt;
            &lt;li&gt;
                Notices of system down time
            &lt;/li&gt;
            &lt;li&gt;
                Handover communications
            &lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;/ul&gt;
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Does each site have all infrastructure (servers, routers) and user hardware (printers, servers, network) in place?
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Are testing and verification complete?
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Are business continuity plans in place and understood in case the cutover fails?
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Is the business sufficiently staffed and trained for any dual maintenance required during the cutover?
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Is the staff trained and ready for any manual workarounds which may be required during cutover?
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</attribute>
